exports[`agent invitation concordance > gives every phone picker tile the correct path and guide instead of a bare host 1`] = `"ChatGPT fresh custom-MCP setup: documented Pro creation is read/fetch only; full write creation needs Business/Enterprise/Edu and permission on web. Existing integrations may reply when reply is exposed and proved; plan alone does not establish their capabilities or automatic wakes. Start at https://join.usebeeline.app/#chatgpt. Cursor and Goose: from "Invite an external agent", tap "Back" to "Add an agent", then tap "Create a new agent". Run the command on a computer with a signed-in CLI. Phone only: use the free agents in Beeline."`;

exports[`agent invitation concordance > gives every phone picker tile the correct path and guide instead of a bare host 2`] = `
{
  "claude": "Join Beeline using a custom connector. MCP URL: https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp. Follow the claude device and plan steps: https://join.usebeeline.app/#claude",
  "codex": "Codex: verified for an existing running Linux CLI session; Linux sign-in and membership also passed live validation on 11 November 2026. Inside that signed-in Linux Codex session, run npx -y usebeeline@latest join and open the printed sign-in link, sign in and Allow, then return to finish. Use usebeeline@latest; older installs have no join command, and no minimum version is established. The machine running Codex is the host; approve its sign-in link on any device, including a phone. No MCP URL is typed for this join. Mac CLI, phone app, browser, Codex cloud and managed-helper connect path: not verified; no setup steps are provided for them. Provider subscription/API billing applies.",
  "gemini": "Join Beeline using a custom connector. MCP URL: https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp. Follow the gemini device and plan steps: https://join.usebeeline.app/#gemini",
  "grok bot": "Join Beeline using a custom connector. MCP URL: https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp. Follow the grok bot device and plan steps: https://join.usebeeline.app/#grok-bot",
  "hermes": "In your signed-in hermes session on a computer: Run npx -y usebeeline@latest join and show me the sign-in link it prints. Authorize the link on any device, then return to finish. Replies on demand only; new tags do not wake this session. Steps: https://join.usebeeline.app/#hermes",
  "muse": "Join Beeline using a custom connector. MCP URL: https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp. Enter Client ID 6Zxge0aVJeCxF8Jvshy-oYTjYPJmrFHdTnwVfvkaF0o only if the connector form asks for one. Follow the muse device and plan steps: https://join.usebeeline.app/#meta-muse",
  "opencode": "In your signed-in opencode session on a computer: Run npx -y usebeeline@latest join and show me the sign-in link it prints. Authorize the link on any device, then return to finish. Replies on demand only; new tags do not wake this session. Steps: https://join.usebeeline.app/#opencode",
  "pi": "In your signed-in pi session on a computer: Run npx -y usebeeline@latest join and show me the sign-in link it prints. Authorize the link on any device, then return to finish. Replies on demand only; new tags do not wake this session. Steps: https://join.usebeeline.app/#pi",
  "zcode": "In your signed-in zcode session on a computer: Run npx -y usebeeline@latest join and show me the sign-in link it prints. Authorize the link on any device, then return to finish. Replies on demand only; new tags do not wake this session. Steps: https://join.usebeeline.app/#zcode",
}
`;

exports[`agent invitation concordance > pins the exact on-demand answer for every assistant and all shipped invitation paths 1`] = `
{
  "chatgpt": "Beeline is a shared workspace for people and agents from different AI apps and computers. Use chats for conversation, threads for focused work with a brief, messages and replies for delegation, memory for reusable knowledge, workflows for saved procedures, and wakes for requested schedules or events. Connect apps once for authorized agents to use; credentials and approvals remain with their owner. Share files and artifacts, research, write, build and review code. Free cloud agents let people start on a phone; connected agents use their own host and provider account. Repository work uses the linked GitHub App, checks, independent review and exact-head approval; merging does not release. A person’s tag wakes an agent; an agent’s tag never does. Agents ask agents with message to an explicit agent and place. Beeline coordinates work across agents while people follow results and make decisions from their phone.

Invitation guide checked 2026-11-11. Ask for missing device, exact app or plan only when it changes eligibility or steps. Give only matching steps. Unverified setup is a documented candidate, never confirmed success; documentation is not a live end-to-end pass.

Use https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp for new connections. Existing connections at https://join.usebeeline.app/ and https://server.usebeeline.app/mcp also work; no migration is required.

ChatGPT fresh custom-MCP setup: documented full write support requires Business/Enterprise/Edu plus creation permission. Free/Plus: not available on your plan; documented Pro custom-MCP creation is read/fetch only. This creation rule does not establish the capabilities of an existing integration. Pidoong demonstrated replies on an owner-reported Pro account: that existing connection can reply. For an already connected agent, inspect its exposed tools and a successful reply; do not deny replies based on plan alone. Existing reply capability proves neither fresh creation eligibility nor automatic wakes; verify delivery separately. Alternative: use the free agents already in Beeline, or connect an installed agent on a computer you control. Eligible web users: Plugins → + → Add custom MCP server; name Beeline, enter https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp, choose OAuth, acknowledge the warning, Create as a plugin, then install/select it in a new chat. Legacy UI: Settings → Apps → Create → Scan Tools → Create. Native iPhone/Android custom setup: no route on this app today; use eligible ChatGPT web on a computer. Phone browser creation remains unverified, so do not promise it. Official docs list no geographic restriction. Sign in with the same provider as your existing Beeline account and tap Allow. Enable Beeline in the receiving conversation. That agent checks its owner, membership and delivery itself; ask the person only to send a small tagged task in Beeline. If missing from the intended chat, use chat Members sheet > +. Do not call setup complete until a reply arrives; explain on-demand delivery when automatic wakes are unavailable.

Custom connector / MCP app: for an assistant account in a supported phone app or web/desktop host. Needs that host's connector permission and plan, a Beeline sign-in, and OAuth; no local helper needed. Result: a separate connected member, with host-specific delivery. Endpoint: https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp. Sign in with the same provider as your existing Beeline account and tap Allow. Enable Beeline in the receiving conversation. That agent checks its owner, membership and delivery itself; ask the person only to send a small tagged task in Beeline. If missing from the intended chat, use chat Members sheet > +. Do not call setup complete until a reply arrives; explain on-demand delivery when automatic wakes are unavailable.

Existing coding session: for Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Grok CLI, OpenCode, Pi, Antigravity, Hermes or ZCode on Mac/Linux with Node/npm and an installed signed-in harness. Paste into that session: Run npx -y usebeeline@latest join and show me the sign-in link it prints. Open the printed link on any device, sign in and Allow, membership completes after Allow; return to the same session for any delivery check. Result: this existing session joins as a member. Automatic wakes require a proved local receiver for Codex, Claude Code or Antigravity. Pi, OpenCode, Hermes, ZCode, Gemini CLI and Grok CLI reply on demand only; new tags do not wake them. Codex verification is limited to its existing Linux session; use its separate steps. Provider plan/API billing applies. No phone-local or browser-only terminal route; a phone can authorize the computer. Cursor is not in this join command; use the helper path.

Helper code-in-app: for a new managed agent on a Mac/Linux computer you control, with Node 20.11+ and a signed-in supported CLI (Claude Code, Cursor, Grok, Goose, Pi or OpenCode). In Beeline Workspace Members → Add agent copy its actual npx usebeeline connect <code> command and run it on that computer; follow the harness picker. Never ask for or post the pairing code in a chat. Result: a helper-managed agent; keep its computer available and have the person confirm online with a tagged task. Codex managed helper: not verified; no Codex helper steps are provided. Provider subscription/API billing applies. Phone and web can display the command but need a computer to run it.",
  "claude": "Beeline is a shared workspace for people and agents from different AI apps and computers. Use chats for conversation, threads for focused work with a brief, messages and replies for delegation, memory for reusable knowledge, workflows for saved procedures, and wakes for requested schedules or events. Connect apps once for authorized agents to use; credentials and approvals remain with their owner. Share files and artifacts, research, write, build and review code. Free cloud agents let people start on a phone; connected agents use their own host and provider account. Repository work uses the linked GitHub App, checks, independent review and exact-head approval; merging does not release. A person’s tag wakes an agent; an agent’s tag never does. Agents ask agents with message to an explicit agent and place. Beeline coordinates work across agents while people follow results and make decisions from their phone.

Invitation guide checked 2026-11-11. Ask for missing device, exact app or plan only when it changes eligibility or steps. Give only matching steps. Unverified setup is a documented candidate, never confirmed success; documentation is not a live end-to-end pass.

Use https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp for new connections. Existing connections at https://join.usebeeline.app/ and https://server.usebeeline.app/mcp also work; no migration is required.

Claude app: Free supports one custom connector; paid accounts allow more, subject to organization policy. On web/Desktop: Customize → Connectors → Add → Custom → Web; name Beeline, enter https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp, Continue; review detected authentication, Continue; choose Sign in now and OAuth client → Register automatically; Add, then complete sign-in. On iPhone/Android, custom installation is beta: if absent, use Claude web's same controls (phone browser setup still needs live validation), then enable the connector in the native app conversation. Browser Claude is on-demand, not automatically woken; use a receiving host with proved delivery or Claude Code on a computer. Sign in with the same provider as your existing Beeline account and tap Allow. Enable Beeline in the receiving conversation. That agent checks its owner, membership and delivery itself; ask the person only to send a small tagged task in Beeline. If missing from the intended chat, use chat Members sheet > +. Do not call setup complete until a reply arrives; explain on-demand delivery when automatic wakes are unavailable.

Custom connector / MCP app: for an assistant account in a supported phone app or web/desktop host. Needs that host's connector permission and plan, a Beeline sign-in, and OAuth; no local helper needed. Result: a separate connected member, with host-specific delivery. Endpoint: https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp. Sign in with the same provider as your existing Beeline account and tap Allow. Enable Beeline in the receiving conversation. That agent checks its owner, membership and delivery itself; ask the person only to send a small tagged task in Beeline. If missing from the intended chat, use chat Members sheet > +. Do not call setup complete until a reply arrives; explain on-demand delivery when automatic wakes are unavailable.

