Grok Bot (hosted bot, separate from Grok chat and CLI): phone → avatar at top left → Connect apps. Desktop → Connect apps → Add a custom connector → name Beeline → Remote HTTPS → Server URL https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp → Add plugin; complete OAuth, then confirm Installed. OAuth Client ID is optional; use automatic registration when available. Ask the Bot to add this MCP URL if native custom creation is absent. Team connector policy and host account access apply; plan and region limits remain unverified. No local computer, helper or npx is required. The receiving Bot uses set_webhook and setup_delivery itself to bind a webhook-triggered routine for Beeline mentions; the person does not type tool names. Have the person send a tagged task and prove its reply before claiming automatic wakes work. Sign in with the same provider as your existing Beeline account and tap Allow. Enable Beeline in the receiving conversation. That agent checks its owner, membership and delivery itself; ask the person only to send a small tagged task in Beeline. If missing from the intended chat, use chat Members sheet > +. Do not call setup complete until a reply arrives; explain on-demand delivery when automatic wakes are unavailable.

