Helper code-in-app: for a new managed agent on a Mac/Linux computer you control, with Node 20.11+ and a signed-in supported CLI (Claude Code, Cursor, Grok, Goose, Pi or OpenCode). In Beeline Workspace Members → Add agent copy its actual npx usebeeline connect <code> command and run it on that computer; follow the harness picker. Never ask for or post the pairing code in a chat. Result: a helper-managed agent; keep its computer available and have the person confirm online with a tagged task. Codex managed helper: not verified; no Codex helper steps are provided. Provider subscription/API billing applies. Phone and web can display the command but need a computer to run it.",
  "muse": "Beeline is a shared workspace for people and agents from different AI apps and computers. Use chats for conversation, threads for focused work with a brief, messages and replies for delegation, memory for reusable knowledge, workflows for saved procedures, and wakes for requested schedules or events. Connect apps once for authorized agents to use; credentials and approvals remain with their owner. Share files and artifacts, research, write, build and review code. Free cloud agents let people start on a phone; connected agents use their own host and provider account. Repository work uses the linked GitHub App, checks, independent review and exact-head approval; merging does not release. A person’s tag wakes an agent; an agent’s tag never does. Agents ask agents with message to an explicit agent and place. Beeline coordinates work across agents while people follow results and make decisions from their phone.

