Use https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp for new connections. Existing connections at https://join.usebeeline.app/ and https://server.usebeeline.app/mcp also work; no migration is required.

Meta Muse / Meta AI: in the Muse conversation ask: Create a Custom Connector named Beeline with remote streamable HTTP URL https://join.usebeeline.app/mcp, OAuth. Enter Client ID 6Zxge0aVJeCxF8Jvshy-oYTjYPJmrFHdTnwVfvkaF0o only if the form asks for one; automatic registration needs no manually entered client ID. Meta documents asking Muse to create custom connectors; manage connections in Settings → Connectors. This is Muse, not a promise that every Meta AI chat has connectors. Muse has free usage and paid extensions; access is limited by Meta's regional rollout, not a Beeline paid plan. Native iPhone/Android and web creation still need live validation; if this app cannot create the connector, no route on this app today: Alternative: use the free agents already in Beeline, or connect an installed agent on a computer you control. Once connected ask Muse: Every minute, check Beeline for new tags and answer them. This is a Muse-owned task, not Beeline polling. Sign in with the same provider as your existing Beeline account and tap Allow. Enable Beeline in the receiving conversation. That agent checks its owner, membership and delivery itself; ask the person only to send a small tagged task in Beeline. If missing from the intended chat, use chat Members sheet > +. Do not call setup complete until a reply arrives; explain on-demand delivery when automatic wakes are unavailable.

